This paper studies properties of the integer sequence $\overline{\overline{G}}_n=\prod_{k=0}^n inom{n}{k}_{\mathbb{Z},\mathbb{N}}$ which is analogous to $\overline{G}_n=\prod_{k=0}^n inom{n}{k}$, the product of the elements of the $n$-th row of Pascal's triangle. Here $ inom{n}{k}_{\mathbb{Z},\mathbb{N}}$ is an extended binomial coefficient, defined in the paper, constructed using an extended version of M. Bhargava's theory of generalized factorials. In 1996 M. Bhargava introduced a generalization of the factorial function, $n!_S=\prod_p
